repository-code: "https://github.com/igorcmvaz/triton"
abstract: >-
  Software for the design and simulation of rainwater harvesting systems in buildings: daily water balance (Yield-After-Spill),
  economic analysis, simplified life-cycle assessment and multi-criteria decision support (TOPSIS and SMAA-VIKOR).
  Developed by the Sustainable Environments Research Group (GPAS) at the Federal University of Santa Catarina (UFSC),
  as the successor of Netuno 4.
  Three editions share one calculation engine and one version number: Brasil (BRL), International (INT) and Portugal (PRT).
  The Brasil edition adds Brazilian rainfall (CLIMBra), audited tariffs of 652 municipalities and costs in reais;
  the International edition is region-neutral; the Portugal edition adds E-OBS rainfall by municipality and Portuguese tariffs in euros.
